From 137575d96819bbb71d344f07b01b28504cb1962c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: parakeet dev <parakeet@local>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 00:22:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: fused LayerNorm + affine (NORM+MUL[+ADD]) + per-op
 instrumentation

Add a fused plain-LayerNorm-with-affine kernel (layer_norm_f32) mirroring the
existing rms_norm_f32 fusion: computes mean+var, then (x-mean)*inv_std[*gamma][+beta]
in one fp32 kernel. Byte-exact with running GGML_OP_NORM ->
GGML_OP_MUL(gamma) -> GGML_OP_ADD(beta) as separate nodes (same fp32 reduction
and same fp32 affine). Collapses 3 nodes -> 1 per LayerNorm in captured graphs.

- norm.cu: layer_norm_f32<do_multiply,do_add> + layer_norm_mul_f32_cuda launcher
  + ggml_cuda_op_norm_fused[_add] entry points.
- norm.cuh: declarations for the two entry points.
- ggml-cuda.cu: GGML_OP_NORM branch in ggml_cuda_can_fuse (mirrors the RMS_NORM
  branch) + dispatch in ggml_cuda_try_fuse.

Also adds gated per-op-type and graph-launch CUDA-event instrumentation
(PARAKEET_PEROP_TIMING, PARAKEET_GPU_TIMING), default off, zero behavior change.
